Fix off-by-one in hunk header parsing

The unified diff parser treated a zero-length range ("@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@")
as starting at line 1 of the old file, which shifted every line number
in newly created files by one. Parse the count separately and only
subtract one from the start when the count is non-zero.

Also add regression tests for empty old/new ranges and for hunks that
end exactly at end of file without a trailing newline.

Fixes #412

